From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:45:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Install the eSpeak NG library on the partition of its
 application

The app is installed on the product partition and does not embed its
libraries, so Soong installs its JNI library as a file of its own. The
library had no partition of its own and went to system, which the
product's generic system rule keeps free of the device makefile's own
files, and the analysis of the image build stopped on it. The library
now installs on the product partition with the application that loads
it, by the module's own partition property.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Android.bp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index c19d7b3b64026ff250431aaaf522ddd5e3e4eaa4..0c610171c58cbe4bbdb54d5d8802181bd9bd1948 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -208,10 +208,12 @@ cc_binary_host {
     ],
 }
 
-// The JNI library of the app.
+// The JNI library of the app. The app is installed on the product partition and
+// does not embed its libraries, so the library installs there with it.
 cc_library_shared {
     name: "espeak_ng_ttsespeak",
     stem: "libttsespeak",
+    product_specific: true,
     defaults: ["espeak_ng_device"],
     licenses: ["external_espeak_ng_app_license"],
     stl: "c++_static",
